Desktop Linux keeps the V4L2 encoder on CPU NV12.

Mesa GBM rejects NV12, and headless ozone exports no dmabuf, so the
WebCodecs adapter stays on shared memory. The encoder's image processor
writes a CPU frame and queues it as USERPTR. apple-ave copies that
pointer during QBUF, so any directly readable frame is usable. ChromeOS
still uses the platform layout and DMA-BUF.

--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
